Z||000000||Rodrv6||02-08-2001||06:16 PM||||I recently got an 88 GT with 133,000 miles and am thinking about going through the engine in the near future.  The car is totally stock and I'm really not interested in any any super mods.  However, if the cylinders on this engine need to be rebored, than the idea of upgrading it to a 3.1 might be appealling.  My question is this--can I keep the stock injectors or would I need to upgrade them to higher flow injectors?  The engine would remain stock except for the displacement.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||02-08-2001||07:14 PM||||Seeing that you have an 88 your flywheel is reuable, the things that would need to be changed are pistons,crank and maybe an adjustable fuel pressure regualtor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-08-2001||09:31 PM||||i've got a set of flow matched 2.8 intectors from the SE. they'll support 240hp... let me know when you need em... we'll figure somthing out   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <BR> <A HREF="http://www.rceng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rceng.com</A>   -  they cleaned em up for me.. then i just ordered a bigger set and used them instead...<P><BR>we need to dyno the car before you dive into it! for a good before and after picture...||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||02-08-2001||11:18 PM||||If you are going to the trouble I would suggest a 3.4 in place of the stock engine.<BR>The 93/95 3.4 V6 once installed looks just like the stock setup.<BR>The only people that will know that you have replaced your worn out 2.8 with the 3.4 is you and your mechanic.<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
